# f1 = add, f2 = called, f3 = the getter
# The same getter as in a-getter-that-a-written-descriptor-lays-for-good-is-proven-once-it-is-laid.ir, written as an entry of a map. The reader of the map read its halves already; it had no word for the flags,
# so the access bore no form (the slot was planned plain and the field left it at the definition) and the change was no descriptor in sight. Both are said now where the flags are written constants.
# The object stays in sight, so every caller of the getter is known. Where the object leaves, the getter leaves with it: getter-leaves-with-its-object.ir.
